# Line endings, once, for every platform.
#
# Without this file git applies the contributor's core.autocrlf, so a Windows
# checkout turns every text file into CRLF. That is invisible for compilers and
# invisible in `git status` (git compares after normalising), but tests that
# compare bytes (rendered frames, installers run with sh) then fail on Windows
# while the file looks unchanged. Normalise on the way in, hand every platform
# the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.pyc binary
*.zip binary
